+#ifdef M4R_MEASURE
+// MEASUREMENT ONLY (contrib/m4r-measure, measurement-build.patch): the worst-case hook. With
+// m4r_measure_worst set (M4R_WORST=1, read once at startup by bitcoind_m4r_measure), every proof first
+// has a copy of itself with chall3 = ff..ff verified, the most expensive invalid proof for its statement
+// and message (SPEC.md section 11: after step 6 the work is fixed but for one conditional XOR per set
+// bit of chall3), and then itself; the result is the proof's own. So every check does at least the work
+// of any invalid proof that reaches R7, and a block of valid proofs at least the work of the same block
+// with any of them invalid, since validation stops at the first failure.
+int m4r_measure_worst{0};
+extern int m4r_measure_count; // src/crypto/mldsa44.cpp: the counters count only while it is set
+namespace {
+std::atomic<uint64_t> g_worst_verifications{0};
